From: CoreELEC
Subject: [PATCH] Don't wake the TV in response to a routing change while it is in standby

AVRs (seen on Denon AVR-X1800H) broadcast a ROUTING_CHANGE pointing at
their active input as part of their power-down sequence when the TV goes
to standby. SetActiveRoute answered that with a full one touch play -
including IMAGE_VIEW_ON to a TV libCEC knows went to standby moments
earlier - powering the TV right back on.

Seen with Kodi's "stop playback on TV standby": stopping the stream makes
the AVR (re)announce its routing ~1.5s after the TV standby broadcast, and
the TV turns back on immediately after being switched off.

Only skip the activation while the cached TV power status is standby or
in transition to standby; the status is refreshed by the TV's own traffic
(a TV-initiated routing change sets it to 'on' before SetActiveRoute runs),
so genuine input switches still activate as before. A TV switching to us
from standby uses SET_STREAM_PATH, which is handled separately and sends
no IMAGE_VIEW_ON.

Applies on top of libcec-001-fix-active-source-on-routing-change.patch.

---
 src/libcec/devices/CECBusDevice.cpp | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/libcec/devices/CECBusDevice.cpp b/src/libcec/devices/CECBusDevice.cpp
--- a/src/libcec/devices/CECBusDevice.cpp
+++ b/src/libcec/devices/CECBusDevice.cpp
@@ -1236,8 +1236,16 @@
   CCECBusDevice* newRoute = m_processor->GetDeviceByPhysicalAddress(iRoute, true);
   if (newRoute && newRoute->IsHandledByLibCEC() && (!ActiveSourceSent() || !newRoute->IsActiveSource()))
   {
-    // routing to our device - activate it
-    newRoute->ActivateSource();
+    // routing to our device - activate it, unless the TV is in standby or on its
+    // way there. AVRs broadcast a routing change while powering down along with
+    // the TV; answering that with 'image view on' would wake the TV right back up
+    CCECBusDevice* tv = m_processor->GetDevice(CECDEVICE_TV);
+    cec_power_status tvStatus = tv ? tv->GetCurrentPowerStatus() : CEC_POWER_STATUS_UNKNOWN;
+    if (tvStatus == CEC_POWER_STATUS_STANDBY ||
+        tvStatus == CEC_POWER_STATUS_IN_TRANSITION_ON_TO_STANDBY)
+      LIB_CEC->AddLog(CEC_LOG_DEBUG, "not activating '%s' on routing change: TV is '%s'", newRoute->GetLogicalAddressName(), ToString(tvStatus));
+    else
+      newRoute->ActivateSource();
   }
   else if (newRoute && !newRoute->IsHandledByLibCEC())
   {
